T:Que Sera, Sera
C:Jay Livingston and Ray Evans, 1956
N:Best-effort version, not verified against a second source. Melody is the
N:upper voice of a choral arrangement MIDI (hamienet.com), moved up a whole
N:step so the lowest note is not below C4. Chords come from that
N:arrangement's piano and bass. The lead line is least certain in bars 10-15,
N:where the arrangement's voices split.
